# NebulaForge

NebulaForge is a lightweight automation framework designed for developers who value clean architecture and modular design.

## Features

- Modular architecture
- Fast and lightweight
- Easy configuration
- Extensible plugin system
- Cross-platform support

## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/NebulaForge.git
cd NebulaForge
python main.py
NebulaForge/
│── main.py
│── config.py
│── requirements.txt
│── README.md
└── core/
    ├── engine.py
    ├── utils.py
    └── plugins.py

### Python Code (`main.py`)
```python
from datetime import datetime

class NebulaForge:
    def __init__(self):
        self.name = "NebulaForge"
        self.version = "1.0.0"

    def start(self):
        print(f"{self.name} v{self.version}")
        print("Automation Engine Started")
        print(f"Started at: {datetime.now()}")

    def run_task(self, task):
        print(f"Running task: {task}")
        print("Task completed successfully.")

if __name__ == "__main__":
    app = NebulaForge()
    app.start()
    app.run_task("System Initialization")

    def start(self):
        print(f"{self.name} v{self.version}")
        print("Automation Engine Started")
        print(f"Started at: {datetime.now()}")

